{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patchset 5 LLM-Review remediation prepared locally and amended into the Gerrit commit. No push performed.\n\nScope:\n- Added real tests for `_refresh_rates`, `_normalise`, and `_metered_spend` instead of asserting loader stubs.\n- Fixed the dual-signal outage deadlock: a fail-closed telemetry outage trip is still enforced for that UTC day, but if the next UTC day still has both spend signals unavailable, the deny policy is released and the handler records that release so the same unavailable-only condition does not immediately re-trip. If either signal later reports cap-level spend, enforcement can attach again. This balances the asymmetric failures: failing to enforce is financial exposure, so the first unavailable-only trip remains fail-closed; failing to release is an access outage, so an outage is not allowed to be both the cause of enforcement and the evidence for sustaining enforcement indefinitely.\n\nRED / teeth evidence:\n- Dual-outage pre-fix regression failed against the unmodified release guard:\n  `FAILED tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_dual_signal_outage_trip_releases_on_next_utc_day`\n  `assert second_result[\"deny_attached\"] is False`\n  `E       assert True is False`\n- `_normalise` teeth check, temporarily changed to strip only the first matching prefix:\n  `FAILED tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_normalise_strips_stacked_single_and_no_prefixes`\n  `E       AssertionError: assert 'anthropicclaudesonnet46' == 'claudesonnet46'`\n- `_refresh_rates` teeth check, temporarily changed aggregation to return an empty map:\n  `FAILED tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_refresh_rates_derives_rates_from_positive_cost_and_quantity`\n  `E       AssertionError: assert {} == {'USE1-model-input-tokens': ..., 'USE1-model-output-tokens': ...}`\n- `_metered_spend` teeth check, temporarily changed pricing accumulation to add nothing:\n  `FAILED tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_prices_known_and_unknown_model_tokens`\n  `E       AssertionError: assert 0.0 == <synthetic expected spend expression>`\n\nGREEN / local gates:\n- `python -m pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -v`: PASS, all 27 tests passed.\n- `make lint`: PASS after Ruff formatted the touched test file; rerun passed.\n- `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check`: PASS; active mechanisms unchanged, pre-existing admitted entries remain admitted.\n- `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`: PASS; no new or increased complexity.\n- `terraform fmt -check && terraform validate`: PASS; configuration valid.\n\nLeft-alone advisories for separate tickets:\n- `_metered_spend` still cannot distinguish genuinely zero usage from missing per-model series.\n- `_ce_spend_today` still assumes a present `Total` object when results exist.\n- The state SSM parameter remains a string-sized runtime state blob while rates can grow.\n- The runtime state parameter remains out-of-band from Terraform.\n- The budget name still changes when the configured cap value changes, so replacement semantics remain.\n- Remaining Gerrit advisories not listed in this ticket comment were intentionally left untouched."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789773333366515215,"uuid":"6c6202cb-225a-4ab7-9f82-80af3802beaa"}